  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "record",
    "description": "Record something the user must see in the /inbox pane, and still say it in your reply. Use it in the turn you raise it, once for each thing.\n- question: a decision, approval or piece of information only the user has, which you need before you go on. Give options, and rec when you recommend one. This includes an act you hold until they say so, such as \"say when you want those committed\".\n- task: a step only the user can do, such as signing in or running a command with their password. Put the commands, files and links in steps.\n- finding: something outside the current task that deserves their attention. It waits in the Findings tab of the /inbox pane until it is closed, and the user can ask you to address it or discuss it. Record what a careful senior engineer would flag to a teammate, once you have checked it. Leave out style nits, anything the user already decided, todos or ideas the user mentioned, problems in your own change, progress, and anything only the user can do or decide: handle those in your reply, or record them as a question or task.\nDo not record rhetorical questions, offers to continue when continuing is the default, FYIs, or invitations to look at finished work."
   },
